1
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:12,920
It's okay, let's move on

2
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:18,500
In the night of the night,
the clouds are coming

3
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:22,760
The clouds are coming, and
look at the light of the sky

4
00:01:25,420 --> 00:01:26,250
If we see the moon,

5
00:01:26,333 --> 00:01:31,157
we'll see the moon We'll
see the moon in the future

6
00:01:31,240 --> 00:01:34,077
So I'll

7
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:41,160
take

8
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:52,650
this time to

9
00:01:52,733 --> 00:01:54,248
explain how the race works.

10
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:58,237
The course consists of one lap
around Long Ring Long Land.

11
00:01:58,320 --> 00:02:01,360
It may sound easy, but
believe me, it's not.

12
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:05,717
If your boat sinks, your team is
immediately disqualified from the race.

13
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:07,000
Oh, yeah! Weapons?

14
00:02:07,180 --> 00:02:08,010
They're allowed!

15
00:02:08,093 --> 00:02:11,017
Guns, cannons, explosives,
anything you can think of!

16
00:02:11,100 --> 00:02:15,865
If that sounds unfair, then you've got no
right at all to call yourself a pirate!

17
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:18,080
Go, Portia!

18
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:22,140
Yeah, drown that long
nose! Who, me? That's it!

19
00:02:22,260 --> 00:02:23,680
We have to win this now!

20
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:25,194
Drowning is fair play.

21
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:26,110
It's in the rules.

22
00:02:26,193 --> 00:02:27,797
I'm excited about this! What?

23
00:02:27,880 --> 00:02:28,860
about losing.

24
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:30,937
Now pay close attention, Usopp.

25
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:34,057
If anything happens to those
two ladies, I'll eviscerate you.

26
00:02:34,140 --> 00:02:35,797
We are going to win this race.

27
00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:36,710
I know it.

28
00:02:36,793 --> 00:02:39,117
Wow, they think they
have a chance of winning.

29
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:41,757
Let the fools think whatever
they want to think, Porcha.

30
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:43,517
We'll sink them right off the bat.

31
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:44,430
Right, Monda?

32
00:02:44,900 --> 00:02:45,880
Hey, fool!

33
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:47,790
Fool!

34
00:02:47,873 --> 00:02:49,837
He honestly thinks they're going to win.

35
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:50,750
What a riot.

36
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:53,177
No one's ever beat the Foxy Pirates.

37
00:02:53,260 --> 00:02:55,797
I doubt this race will
even last five minutes.

38
00:02:55,880 --> 00:02:56,710
Am I right?

39
00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:58,760
You know it.

40
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:04,660
To ensure you don't get lost, we're
providing each team with an eternal pose.

41
00:03:05,760 --> 00:03:06,780
Get lost?

42
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:10,221
What's this doofus talking about?

43
00:03:10,420 --> 00:03:11,917
Why would we leave the island?

44
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,297
We're taking the inside
track the whole way.

45
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:16,439
I'm afraid it won't be that simple.

46
00:03:16,820 --> 00:03:20,160
Now, on your marks, Jeopardy!

47
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:22,437
Just tell me why it won't be simple.

48
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:23,350
Trust me.

49
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:26,800
Tell me why.

50
00:03:30,940 --> 00:03:32,597
I've got a terrible feeling about this!

51
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:35,077
No, quit babbling and tell us why already!

52
00:03:37,180 --> 00:03:38,360
Push, push, push!

53
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:42,420
Time to reveal the secret of our book.

54
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:44,680
It's got a sneaky little burpee.

55
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:48,910
Oh, no!

56
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:50,297
We didn't get far enough!

57
00:03:50,380 --> 00:03:51,477
What's the big deal?

58
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:52,680
It's just a barrel.

59
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:54,780
No, not me! Don't!

60
00:04:03,040 --> 00:04:04,569
And they've been released!

61
00:04:04,740 --> 00:04:05,570
Look at that!

62
00:04:05,653 --> 00:04:06,483
Kaboom!

63
00:04:06,566 --> 00:04:07,396
The old barrel mines!

64
00:04:07,479 --> 00:04:08,891
The Coaster's Chump Card!

65
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:14,860
See you later, chumps!

66
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,077
You're supposed to avoid
thinking, you know!

67
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:18,219
Wish us good luck!

68
00:04:22,020 --> 00:04:25,960
All right, Capote, give them a
taste of your fishman karate. Yeah!

69
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:28,300
Surface Splitter!

70
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:34,120
The boat's breaking apart!

71
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:36,760
Our balance!

72
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:38,548
We've got to stay balanced!

73
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:41,780
Take this! Eat flame!

74
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:43,180
No thanks.

75
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:45,940
All right. Ocho flue.

76
00:04:47,180 --> 00:04:49,080
What the? Capote!

77
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:51,360
And now, flip.

78
00:04:54,080 --> 00:04:55,920
Perfect! Now's our chance!

79
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:58,497
Usopp, jump in the
water and pull the boat!

80
00:04:58,580 --> 00:04:59,410
Hurry!

81
00:04:59,493 --> 00:05:00,417
Are you crazy?!

82
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:02,441
Khaboudi, Monda, get it together!

83
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:03,900
Come on, pedal!

84
00:05:04,060 --> 00:05:06,997
I think it's about time that
we get to work, Hamburg.

85
00:05:07,080 --> 00:05:07,910
Really?

86
00:05:07,993 --> 00:05:09,916
Oh, boy, I was hoping you'd say that.

87
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:11,240
All right, folks,

88
00:05:11,440 --> 00:05:15,737
currently in the lead of the race is
everyone's all-time favorite, the Cutie Wagon.

89
00:05:15,820 --> 00:05:17,717
Right behind them in second
place is the Barry Tyler.

90
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:18,677
Hey, wait a sec.

91
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:20,277
Why don't we just use one of your dials?

92
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:21,360
Oh, good idea.

93
00:05:21,580 --> 00:05:23,698
We can give this breath dial a shot.

94
00:05:25,920 --> 00:05:27,537
We were going faster before.

95
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:29,477
Well, do you have a jet dial on you?

96
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:31,317
Come on, you know how rare those are.

97
00:05:31,400 --> 00:05:33,537
We're talking about losing a crew member.

98
00:05:33,620 --> 00:05:34,450
He's right.

99
00:05:34,533 --> 00:05:35,680
We can't lose here.

100
00:05:35,980 --> 00:05:37,804
There's just too much at stake.

101
00:05:37,900 --> 00:05:41,337
If we lose, I know they'll
definitely take me first.

102
00:05:41,420 --> 00:05:42,600
I just know it.

103
00:05:43,480 --> 00:05:44,360
Oh, why?

104
00:05:44,460 --> 00:05:45,780
Why am I so cute?

105
00:05:46,480 --> 00:05:47,310
Whatever.

106
00:05:47,393 --> 00:05:48,729
You just keep on dreaming.

107
00:05:52,180 --> 00:05:54,457
Robin, this isn't the
best time for reading.

108
00:05:54,540 --> 00:05:55,860
I'm rowing, too.

109
00:05:56,140 --> 00:05:59,437
Well, yeah, your hands are, but
you're not really focused on it.

110
00:05:59,520 --> 00:06:00,380
Right, Robin.

111
00:06:00,700 --> 00:06:02,697
You don't want to end up like me, right?

112
00:06:02,780 --> 00:06:03,800
Better work hard.

113
00:06:04,020 --> 00:06:05,200
I am working hard.

114
00:06:05,660 --> 00:06:07,900
Yeah, working hard in archaeology.

115
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:10,757
What do you think?

116
00:06:10,840 --> 00:06:14,397
Should we head for the finish line,
or should we enjoy seeking them first?

117
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:17,997
I enjoy casually scrolling through the
finish line as much as the next guy,

118
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:20,256
but I want to make that chick suffer.

119
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:23,037
Simply winning this thing ain't
going to be enough for me anymore.

120
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:24,100
What the?

121
00:06:24,740 --> 00:06:26,152
How's this work for you?

122
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:27,479
Excellent, Robert.

123
00:06:27,740 --> 00:06:29,328
That is downright cheating.

124
00:06:30,580 --> 00:06:31,410
Let go.

125
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:34,400
It's too bad they already noticed.

126
00:06:34,880 --> 00:06:35,720
Capote, no.

127
00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:39,257
They're going to pay.

128
00:06:39,340 --> 00:06:41,157
Let's just keep paddling with all we got.

129
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:44,437
We've got to try and catch up to them
before they get an even bigger lead on us.

130
00:06:44,520 --> 00:06:48,200
Well then, I guess I'll be
seeking them after all. Oh.

131
00:06:48,940 --> 00:06:49,770
Hm?

132
00:06:50,700 --> 00:06:54,397
They're now approaching the most
fearsome obstacles of the course,

133
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:56,000
the Long Coral Reef.

134
00:06:56,140 --> 00:06:58,437
And just beyond that
foreboding and difficult patch

135
00:06:58,520 --> 00:07:01,380
is the dreaded Long Ring
Whirlpool of Long King.

136
00:07:01,760 --> 00:07:03,457
Can they overcome these hurdles?

137
00:07:03,540 --> 00:07:05,480
And oh, we'll all be.

138
00:07:05,960 --> 00:07:06,880
What now?

139
00:07:07,100 --> 00:07:08,460
Talk about unexpected.

140
00:07:10,960 --> 00:07:13,860
It's Full Dash Hamburg at full speed.

141
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:17,177
And riding atop him is the
master of obstruction himself.

142
00:07:17,260 --> 00:07:21,613
the scourge of fairness, and the
greatest scoundrel of all time, our boss,

143
00:07:21,840 --> 00:07:23,980
Silver Fox Foxy!

144
00:07:24,660 --> 00:07:25,490
It's him!

145
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:28,460
I've just come up with an evil idea.

146
00:07:29,560 --> 00:07:31,520
This race is really heating up.

147
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:34,637
The next course obstacle, the
long coral reef is dead ahead,

148
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:37,177
leading the race is Portia
and the cutie wagon.

149
00:07:37,260 --> 00:07:41,400
Look, that weird reef is causing
some unusual currents to form.

150
00:07:41,840 --> 00:07:43,840
Going in blind is not a good idea.

151
00:07:44,520 --> 00:07:48,000
Ugh, I can't believe this stupid
race has lasted this long.

152
00:07:48,420 --> 00:07:50,480
We're counting on you, Monda. Yeah!

153
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:51,917
And don't forget,

154
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,717
there's someone on land looking for
every opportunity to sabotage this race.

155
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:58,180
Our boss, Silver Fox Foxy.

156
00:07:58,360 --> 00:08:00,654
Just what does he have in store for us?

157
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:08,660
All right, hope you like fish and noodles,
free of charge. For real? Oh, how cool.

158
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:09,690
Thank you.

159
00:08:11,920 --> 00:08:15,257
Why is it that all the good cooks
like you were already taken?

160
00:08:15,340 --> 00:08:17,700
Your curly-cute eyebrows are so cute.

161
00:08:18,520 --> 00:08:22,320
You know, I gotta say, I won't
mind if I get Davey back.

162
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:25,857
Hey, we need another
round of drinks down here.

163
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:28,097
The brew is endless,
so drink all you want.

164
00:08:28,180 --> 00:08:29,637
Thanks, you guys are all right.

165
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:31,220
Yeah, get him, boss.

166
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:33,737
It's only a matter of time.

167
00:08:33,820 --> 00:08:35,232
Wait, wait, what's this?

168
00:08:35,940 --> 00:08:38,980
Come on, Nami, keep
rowing. Not yet. Not yet!

169
00:08:39,160 --> 00:08:40,577
They're getting further ahead of us!

170
00:08:40,660 --> 00:08:41,490
I know, okay?

171
00:08:41,573 --> 00:08:42,833
We're not going in yet!

172
00:08:42,960 --> 00:08:45,317
The Cutie Wagon takes
advantage of this opportunity

173
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:48,420
and plunges forward into
the long coral reef!

174
00:08:48,660 --> 00:08:50,540
Let's go, Monda! Sure!

175
00:08:51,800 --> 00:08:54,080
Hey, wait a minute! What's happening?

176
00:08:54,880 --> 00:08:55,710
Monda!

177
00:08:57,320 --> 00:08:59,557
Uh-oh, they came back. What?!

178
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:02,097
The Cutie Wagon has been
pushed back out of the reef!

179
00:09:02,180 --> 00:09:03,477
What's happening down there?!

180
00:09:03,560 --> 00:09:04,800
I don't understand!

181
00:09:05,320 --> 00:09:08,791
See, I knew there was something
weird about those currents.

182
00:09:09,820 --> 00:09:10,650
Now!

183
00:09:10,780 --> 00:09:12,057
Let's get moving, Usopp!

184
00:09:12,140 --> 00:09:12,970
Right!

185
00:09:13,053 --> 00:09:14,660
Let's try this again, Monda!

186
00:09:14,880 --> 00:09:15,939
Come on, this way!

187
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:21,260
Hey! What's that?

188
00:09:25,700 --> 00:09:26,737
Ha-ha!

189
00:09:26,820 --> 00:09:28,077
And there you have it!

190
00:09:28,160 --> 00:09:31,278
The devilish interference
we've all been waiting for!

191
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:33,300
Some kind of smokescreen!

192
00:09:34,140 --> 00:09:36,434
Now the reef will be far too dangerous!

193
00:09:38,020 --> 00:09:39,257
And there you have it!

194
00:09:39,340 --> 00:09:41,105
Operation Whiteout successful!

195
00:09:41,540 --> 00:09:45,797
Let's see how you navigate through this
reef when you can't even see through it!

196
00:09:45,880 --> 00:09:47,174
You're sure it worked?

197
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:51,857
What the hell?!

198
00:09:51,940 --> 00:09:54,760
They made it through
with no trouble at all!

199
00:09:54,980 --> 00:09:56,377
How is that possible?!

200
00:09:56,460 --> 00:09:57,440
I called it.

201
00:09:57,560 --> 00:09:59,089
What about the duty wagon?

202
00:09:59,740 --> 00:10:00,640
Oh no!

203
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:02,857
Seems they've been pushed back again!

204
00:10:02,940 --> 00:10:04,917
Hey, the boat is moving on its own!

205
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:06,077
What's going on here, Nami?

206
00:10:06,160 --> 00:10:08,760
This place is a maze
of currents. Currents?

207
00:10:09,500 --> 00:10:10,330
Right.

208
00:10:10,413 --> 00:10:12,637
That giant whirlpool
ahead of us is causing

209
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:14,837
smaller whirlpools to
form within the reef?

210
00:10:14,920 --> 00:10:16,677
resulting in these strange currents.

211
00:10:16,760 --> 00:10:19,757
Doesn't matter if we can't
see, their course won't change.

212
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:21,537
As long as we take the right entrance,

213
00:10:21,620 --> 00:10:24,497
these currents will guide the
boat along all by themselves.

214
00:10:24,580 --> 00:10:25,410
Incredible!

215
00:10:25,493 --> 00:10:26,323
You're a miracle!

216
00:10:26,406 --> 00:10:27,497
That's what you can do when you've got the

217
00:10:27,580 --> 00:10:29,697
best navigator on the
Grand Line in your crew!

218
00:10:29,780 --> 00:10:30,610
Take that!

219
00:10:30,900 --> 00:10:31,820
Damn it!

220
00:10:34,100 --> 00:10:36,394
But they won't be celebrating for long.

221
00:10:36,620 --> 00:10:40,620
Once they're out of the reef, they
head straight into the long ring.

222
00:10:41,120 --> 00:10:44,040
Usopp, stop freaking out
and use it. Use what?

223
00:10:44,420 --> 00:10:45,460
The impact dial.

224
00:10:45,820 --> 00:10:47,837
But I don't have it with me, though.

225
00:10:47,920 --> 00:10:49,400
Yeah, then what's this?

226
00:10:50,180 --> 00:10:51,010
What's that?

227
00:10:51,093 --> 00:10:52,480
We're dead. How did you?

228
00:10:52,780 --> 00:10:53,720
Come on, hurry.

229
00:10:53,900 --> 00:10:56,897
If you don't use it soon, we'll be
sucked down into the giant whirlpool.

230
00:10:56,980 --> 00:10:58,457
You know what it's like to use that thing?

231
00:10:58,540 --> 00:11:00,637
Come on, we're running out of time here.

232
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:03,600
So that's why you've
been acting so calm, huh?

233
00:11:03,940 --> 00:11:07,116
You had this plan from the
very beginning, didn't you?

234
00:11:07,380 --> 00:11:08,210
Well...

235
00:11:09,120 --> 00:11:09,950
Oh!

236
00:11:10,033 --> 00:11:12,657
The Barrel Tiger picked
up some tremendous speed!

237
00:11:12,740 --> 00:11:15,077
They're not just going
faster, they're playing!

238
00:11:15,160 --> 00:11:19,100
And with that move, the Barrel
Tiger now has a commanding lead!

239
00:11:19,380 --> 00:11:21,909
Does this mean defeat
for the Beauty Wagon?

240
00:11:22,080 --> 00:11:23,920
We were way too easy on them!

241
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:25,276
I'm counting on you!

242
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:27,180
Karoo, time!

243
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:30,100
Two fish engines!

244
00:11:31,060 --> 00:11:32,937
They're not out of the race yet!

245
00:11:33,020 --> 00:11:35,557
By fusing fish man muscle
with the fin of a shark,

246
00:11:35,640 --> 00:11:38,077
the cutie wagon has
doubled its engine speed!

247
00:11:38,160 --> 00:11:41,336
They're blazing through the
coral and closing the gap!

248
00:11:42,540 --> 00:11:44,780
The race is now half over!

249
00:11:45,020 --> 00:11:48,080
Meanwhile, the barrel tiger
desperately paddles on!

250
00:11:48,260 --> 00:11:49,520
Usopp, wake up!

251
00:11:49,720 --> 00:11:51,240
Ugh, where am I?

252
00:11:51,400 --> 00:11:52,937
Get off and start paddling!

253
00:11:53,020 --> 00:11:55,549
Your arm seems to be
bending the wrong way.

254
00:11:57,180 --> 00:11:58,397
What is that?

255
00:11:58,480 --> 00:11:59,957
Looks like a course marker.

256
00:12:00,040 --> 00:12:01,537
Turn right, huh?

257
00:12:01,620 --> 00:12:03,417
Guess we'll turn right then.

258
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:06,777
What's this?

259
00:12:06,860 --> 00:12:07,917
She broke it.

260
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:09,837
Our boss is Ploy Number 18.

261
00:12:09,920 --> 00:12:11,960
Operation Life has failed.

262
00:12:12,700 --> 00:12:14,557
What a formidable woman.

263
00:12:14,640 --> 00:12:17,405
Does she not believe in
anything in this world?

264
00:12:18,640 --> 00:12:19,937
She's fell mouth.

265
