Oh, no.

344
00:15:26,053 --> 00:15:27,197
Looks like we sprung a lake.

345
00:15:27,280 --> 00:15:28,110
Don't worry.

346
00:15:28,193 --> 00:15:29,023
We can make it.

347
00:15:29,106 --> 00:15:30,297
We're almost to the goal.

348
00:15:30,380 --> 00:15:31,210
Keep paddling.

349
00:15:31,360 --> 00:15:38,060
Round one of the Davy back fight, the
donut race, is about to come to a close.

350
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:39,880
Oh, Murchin. Come on.

351
00:15:40,220 --> 00:15:41,420
Stay strong, Monda.

352
00:15:41,580 --> 00:15:43,080
We can't let him beat us.

353
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:47,117
We're going to lose if
we don't do something.

354
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:48,780
Bring us up alongside him.

355
00:15:48,900 --> 00:15:49,730
Right, boss.

356
00:15:50,380 --> 00:15:51,400
Robin, baby!

357
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:55,397
Nami, my darling, you look so
hot when you're going fast!

358
00:15:55,480 --> 00:15:58,300
Man, you guys almost
won. What do you mean?

359
00:15:58,440 --> 00:16:00,028
We're totally going to win.

360
00:16:00,580 --> 00:16:01,780
Not so fast.

361
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:03,017
Take a look over there.

362
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:06,260
Our boss is coming. Yeah?
So what? What can he do?

363
00:16:06,460 --> 00:16:08,080
Our boss is just like you.

364
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:09,840
He has Devil Fruit powers.

365
00:16:14,220 --> 00:16:15,640
Slow, slow beam!

366
00:16:25,480 --> 00:16:28,257
And the winner is the cutie wagon.

367
00:16:28,340 --> 00:16:34,577
The hero of the first round of the
Davey Back fight Is our very own idol.

368
00:16:34,660 --> 00:16:36,497
Way to go!

369
00:16:36,580 --> 00:16:37,757
Thank you.

370
00:16:37,840 --> 00:16:39,837
You are the greatest.

371
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:45,857
Looks like we're about
to get a new crew member.

372
00:16:45,940 --> 00:16:48,797
There's nobody that can
beat the Foxy Pirates.

373
00:16:48,880 --> 00:16:50,000
We always win.

374
00:16:53,840 --> 00:16:54,960
Oh, oh, oh.

375
00:16:56,160 --> 00:16:57,278
Hoy, hoy, hoy, hoy.

376
00:16:58,800 --> 00:16:59,630
Befefefefefefe.

377
00:16:59,713 --> 00:17:01,835
Now it's time for you guys to play up.

378
00:17:01,940 --> 00:17:03,764
We are taking one of your crew.

379
00:17:04,380 --> 00:17:05,340
You guys hurt?

380
00:17:05,540 --> 00:17:07,080
Is everybody OK, Robert?

381
00:17:07,280 --> 00:17:08,800
Yes, we're all right.

382
00:17:09,100 --> 00:17:10,957
What the heck happened out there?

383
00:17:11,040 --> 00:17:12,797
I'd like to know the same thing.

384
00:17:12,880 --> 00:17:14,377
We'd all like to know what happened.

385
00:17:14,460 --> 00:17:16,048
Did we really lose somehow?

386
00:17:16,380 --> 00:17:19,377
You looked like you were going to win,
but then you suddenly slowed down?

387
00:17:19,460 --> 00:17:20,636
and they passed you.

388
00:17:23,080 --> 00:17:25,139
There's nothing strange about that.

389
00:17:25,320 --> 00:17:27,660
It was caused by slow-mo photon.

390
00:17:28,060 --> 00:17:31,097
Hey, what did you do to
Nami's team, you smug bastard?

391
00:17:31,180 --> 00:17:32,820
What's a slow-mo photon?

392
00:17:33,140 --> 00:17:36,728
They are particles unlike any
others known to modern science.

393
00:17:37,240 --> 00:17:38,777
Whatever this light touches,

394
00:17:38,860 --> 00:17:43,272
be it an animal, a liquid, a solid, or
even a gas, will lose a fixed amount

395
00:17:43,380 --> 00:17:45,937
of its velocity, while
simultaneously retaining?

396
00:17:46,020 --> 00:17:48,257
all its other energy. You're dumb.

397
00:17:48,340 --> 00:17:49,980
That makes no sense at all.

398
00:17:50,100 --> 00:17:51,260
He just bugged me.

399
00:17:51,500 --> 00:17:52,400
Oh, so you OK?

400
00:17:52,980 --> 00:17:53,810
No way.

401
00:17:54,120 --> 00:17:56,397
Something that ridiculous
is just - Impossible?

402
00:17:56,480 --> 00:17:58,186
Is that what you're thinking?

403
00:17:58,280 --> 00:18:00,280
Surely you know that such a naive,

404
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:03,618
childish claim has no merit
out here on these waters.

405
00:18:03,780 --> 00:18:05,377
Everything they touch slows down.

406
00:18:05,460 --> 00:18:07,277
That's the power of slow-mo photons.

407
00:18:07,360 --> 00:18:08,595
Now that makes sense.

408
00:18:08,840 --> 00:18:10,397
Why didn't you say so before?

409
00:18:10,480 --> 00:18:14,477
After I ate the slow, slow fruit, I became
a slow motion man, capable of producing?

410
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:16,980
these particles from my body. Observe!

411
00:18:20,480 --> 00:18:21,310
Ah!

412
00:18:21,420 --> 00:18:22,940
A floating cannonball!

413
00:18:23,140 --> 00:18:24,560
The slow, slow beam!

414
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:28,640
The effect lasts approximately 30 seconds,

415
00:18:28,820 --> 00:18:31,097
after which the object will
regain its original speed?

416
00:18:31,180 --> 00:18:33,062
as if nothing had ever happened.

417
00:18:36,020 --> 00:18:38,079
Can't believe your eyes, I take it.

418
00:18:39,860 --> 00:18:40,690
Oh, no!

419
00:18:41,700 --> 00:18:42,820
I get it.

420
00:18:42,960 --> 00:18:45,037
So that's why we didn't win the race.

421
00:18:45,120 --> 00:18:48,637
It also explains why they're so
overly confident about these games.

422
00:18:48,720 --> 00:18:50,757
What a joke of a Devil Fruit power.

423
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:51,717
It doesn't matter!

424
00:18:51,800 --> 00:18:52,740
You guys lost!

425
00:18:52,860 --> 00:18:55,237
You know all the rules and
you agree to all the terms!

426
00:18:55,320 --> 00:18:57,100
The donut race is over!

427
00:18:57,360 --> 00:18:59,100
And we are the winners!

428
00:18:59,540 --> 00:19:01,680
Aw, too bad for you guys.

429
00:19:01,820 --> 00:19:03,580
That concludes round one.

430
00:19:03,760 --> 00:19:06,677
And now we shall commence with
the awarding of the prize.

431
00:19:06,760 --> 00:19:10,407
The winning captain will select
a member of the opposing crew.

432
00:19:19,160 --> 00:19:19,990
You...

433
00:19:20,073 --> 00:19:22,140
My first selection is none other than...

434
00:19:23,740 --> 00:19:26,940
You, the doctor, Tonitoni Chopper!

435
00:19:27,460 --> 00:19:28,290
Ha?

436
00:19:28,780 --> 00:19:30,640
Bring him to me at once!

437
00:19:31,640 --> 00:19:32,470
No, no! No!

438
00:19:32,553 --> 00:19:33,383
No!

439
00:19:33,466 --> 00:19:34,296
No!

440
00:19:34,379 --> 00:19:35,209
Chopper!

441
00:19:35,292 --> 00:19:36,122
Such a rare creature.

442
00:19:36,205 --> 00:19:38,368
You're even softer than
I imagined you'd be.

443
00:19:40,140 --> 00:19:41,669
Trust me, I hold him, too.

444
00:19:41,940 --> 00:19:45,260
He's just so damn cute, and he's ours now.

445
00:19:48,480 --> 00:19:49,310
Chopper!

446
00:19:51,320 --> 00:19:53,997
So that creep had his
eyes set on Chopper, huh?

447
00:19:54,080 --> 00:19:57,497
Well, I suppose that he is among
the rarest of rare animals.

448
00:19:57,580 --> 00:19:59,077
Or maybe he collects cute things?

449
00:19:59,160 --> 00:20:01,097
You know, I wouldn't
rule out a fur fetish.

450
00:20:01,180 --> 00:20:02,557
Why does it even matter?

451
00:20:02,640 --> 00:20:03,470
Focus, people!

452
00:20:03,680 --> 00:20:05,857
That freak over there
just took our friend!

453
00:20:05,940 --> 00:20:06,770
You guys.

454
00:20:08,480 --> 00:20:09,640
All right, Dr.

455
00:20:09,800 --> 00:20:11,257
Chopper, enough of all that.

456
00:20:11,340 --> 00:20:12,869
You're one of my crew now.

457
00:20:13,100 --> 00:20:15,237
You need to pledge your loyalty to me.

458
00:20:15,320 --> 00:20:17,940
And you can start by putting on this mask.

459
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:20,840
You guys.

460
00:20:21,740 --> 00:20:23,880
I'm so sorry that we lost Chopper.

461
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,020
We did our best.

462
00:20:25,760 --> 00:20:26,590
Farewell.

463
00:20:27,840 --> 00:20:30,180
He is truly a rarity.

464
00:20:31,080 --> 00:20:32,737
I'm here, you're talking reindeer.

465
00:20:32,820 --> 00:20:33,860
He's so amazing.

466
00:20:34,880 --> 00:20:36,337
We're going to get along great.

467
00:20:36,420 --> 00:20:37,250
Here.

468
00:20:37,333 --> 00:20:38,600
Welcome aboard!

469
00:20:42,540 --> 00:20:43,860
You guys!

470
00:20:44,940 --> 00:20:45,770
Listen!

471
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:48,900
I only went out to sea because of you!

472
00:20:49,200 --> 00:20:52,500
I won't! No! I refuse!

473
00:20:53,520 --> 00:20:55,740
Luffy, you invited me!

474
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:58,440
I said sail to be one of the Straw Hats!

475
00:20:58,560 --> 00:21:02,120
I won't go with them! Please! No!

476
00:21:02,500 --> 00:21:05,097
I am the ship's doctor
of the Straw Hat Pirates!

477
00:21:05,180 --> 00:21:06,840
Doty-doty Chopper!

478
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:10,760
I won't go!

479
00:21:12,700 --> 00:21:14,840
Quit your bellyaching, Chopper.

480
00:21:15,820 --> 00:21:17,020
It's disgraceful.

481
00:21:17,700 --> 00:21:18,740
Uh, Zoro?

482
00:21:19,020 --> 00:21:22,480
You made the choice to set
sail as a pirate. Only you.

483
00:21:22,740 --> 00:21:25,877
And now you have to live with the
consequences of that decision.

484
00:21:25,960 --> 00:21:28,260
We agreed to the terms of this game.

485
00:21:28,600 --> 00:21:31,776
You, Usopp, and everyone
else did the best they could.

486
00:21:32,260 --> 00:21:36,557
But not one pirate worth his salt is
going to sympathize with those tears.

487
00:21:36,640 --> 00:21:41,620
A man would suck it up and quietly
watch the rest of this game.

488
00:21:42,920 --> 00:21:44,240
What's wrong with you?

489
00:21:44,440 --> 00:21:46,675
Don't you know how he must be feeling?

490
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:52,760
Boil me or cook me alive!

491
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:54,882
Give me your worst, you bastard!

492
00:21:56,180 --> 00:21:57,010
Chopper.

493
00:21:57,140 --> 00:21:58,080
That boy.

494
00:21:58,440 --> 00:22:00,557
Whoa, that swordsman is totally awesome!

495
00:22:00,640 --> 00:22:03,220
All right, you teach him a lesson, Zoro!

496
00:22:03,640 --> 00:22:05,160
Yeah, get Chopper back!

497
00:22:05,680 --> 00:22:07,437
Hey, boss, let's take him next.

498
00:22:07,520 --> 00:22:08,577
That reindeer's got guns.

499
00:22:08,660 --> 00:22:10,719
Let's get the second event started.

500
00:22:10,880 --> 00:22:13,260
So inspirational, I can't stop crying.

501
00:22:13,580 --> 00:22:16,168
Yeah, we still have two
rounds left of this.

502
00:22:16,960 --> 00:22:21,195
There's no way we're letting these
jerks take our emergency food supply.

503
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:22,597
Saji, we're counting on you!

504
00:22:22,680 --> 00:22:24,397
The exchange is complete
and the excitement

505
00:22:24,480 --> 00:22:27,177
explodes as the daily
backbite enters round two.

506
00:22:27,260 --> 00:22:29,877
Hey, wasn't Chopper supposed
to be in the second round?

507
00:22:29,960 --> 00:22:31,637
How can he compete if they took him?

508
00:22:31,720 --> 00:22:32,550
Good point.

509
00:22:32,980 --> 00:22:35,237
That's one of the most
thrilling parts of the game.

510
00:22:35,320 --> 00:22:36,237
Remember the rules.

511
00:22:36,320 --> 00:22:38,157
You cannot change your team's roster.

512
00:22:38,240 --> 00:22:40,600
No replacements allowed. In other words,

513
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:44,117
only the remaining two contestants
can participate in round two's game,

514
00:22:44,200 --> 00:22:45,141
the groggy ring.

515
00:22:45,340 --> 00:22:47,497
This gives the foxy
team an early advantage.

516
00:22:47,580 --> 00:22:48,410
What?

517
00:22:48,493 --> 00:22:49,323
That's not fair.

518
00:22:49,406 --> 00:22:50,797
Actually, you could sit this one out, too.

519
00:22:50,880 --> 00:22:53,880
Nah, but feel free to do
the same thing, you loser.

520
00:22:54,080 --> 00:22:57,477
It's hard to believe that they're
going to work together as a team.

521
00:22:57,560 --> 00:22:59,237
What was that? Knock it off!

522
00:22:59,320 --> 00:23:02,137
I will now explain the
rules of the groggy ring.

523
00:23:02,220 --> 00:23:04,577
We have a playing field,
and we have two goals.

524
00:23:04,660 --> 00:23:06,417
Knock the ball into the goal, and you win.

525
00:23:06,500 --> 00:23:08,853
However, the ball isn't actually a ball.

526
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:10,480
The balls are people.

527
00:23:10,920 --> 00:23:13,377
Both teams must select
someone to be the ball.

528
00:23:13,460 --> 00:23:14,636
Make your selection.

529
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:15,830
You heard him.

530
00:23:16,040 --> 00:23:18,981
Which one of you two guys
is going to be the ball?

531
00:23:20,080 --> 00:23:20,910
